# Principal Dams Engineer

Wallingford, UK

At HR Wallingford, we design smart, resilient solutions across the natural and built environments to help everyone live and work more sustainably with water. By harnessing research, data insights and the power of our collective expertise, we help the world to better understand the changing influence and impact of water.

HR Wallingford is not just a workplace; it's a community of exceptional minds pushing the boundaries of conventional thinking. As a not-for-profit company, our focus is on research, innovation, and developing our people, tools, and technology. Here, you'll have the freedom to make long-term decisions that sustain our colleagues, business, and environment.

We are recruiting for a Principal Dams Engineer within our thriving Water and Climate Division, where you will help shape the leadership of our ambitious Dams Sector team. Drawing upon your wealth of experience in the UK reservoir industry, you'll play a pivotal role in the intricate landscape of dam and reservoir engineering.

As a key contributor to our team, your expertise extends across several of the various domains relevant to this team, including hydrology, geotechnics, flood control, hydropower, water supply, risk assessment, and asset management. Collaborate with a diverse team of civil engineers, numerical modellers, and software developers, all committed to crafting innovative solutions for the most complex challenges in the field.

Beyond your core responsibilities, this role offers a unique opportunity to actively engage in, and even lead, ground-breaking research, and development projects. This not only adds depth to your professional journey but also fuels the growth of our business and the dam safety industry.

**Key qualifications and skills**

* A degree in civil engineering, hydrology, or geotechnical engineering;
* Current appointment to the Supervising Engineers Panel;
* Experience of working in the UK reservoir industry;
* Chartered Status (CEng);
* At least 10 years of professional experience related to dams and reservoirs;
* Knowledge of the UK Reservoirs Act 1975 and key industry guidance documents;
* Proven project management skills for studies, design or construction projects;
* An inquisitive nature and interest in leading research and development projects related to dam safety;
* Successful bid writing and business development experience;
* Experience of managing teams;
* Ability to work collaboratively with multi-disciplinary teams;
* Excellent inter-personal and client liaison skills;
* Excellent oral and written communication skills in English.

**Further information**

* Download a full job description and person specification.
* Check out our exceptional benefits at hrwallingford.com/careers.
* A salary from £51,000 - £70,000 dependant on experience
* We understand the importance of a healthy work-life balance and offer both hybrid working and flexi-time. We are also open to exploring other flexible working arrangements, including part-time.
* The closing date for applications is 31 October 2026.

**How to apply**

If you are excited about this role but unsure whether you’re the right fit, we encourage you to apply. We’re also happy to answer any questions by emailing careers@hrwallingford.com

Interested? Please apply providing your CV with covering letter.

# Stock Operations Associate - Celine - Bicester

Published on 07.29.2026

Celine

Retail

Reference: CELI05577

* Place of employment : 

  Bicester, United Kingdom
* Contrat type : 

  Permanent Job
* Required experience : 

  Minimum 3 years
* Work mode : 

  Full Time

* POSITION
* JOB RESPONSIBILITIES
* PROFILE
* ADDITIONAL INFORMATION

Position

### Position

CELINE, founded in 1945 by Céline Vipiana, is an iconic French Leather-Goods, Fashion & Couture House belonging to the LVMH Group. To have a chance of joining CELINE, you must thrive as a team player in a fast-paced environment amongst passionate, agile, and authentic people.

### Job responsibilities

**YOUR WORK ENVIRONMENT**

As stock controller, and part of the operations team in CELINE Bicester, you will participate in back of house operations and you will be in charge of stock management and e-commerce.

**YOUR IMPACT**

* Ensure all internal stock transfers are properly recorded at the time of movement, where necessary find solutions to outstanding, missing or unaccounted items;
* Ensure all products are boxed, labelled and stored correctly in the stockroom and products on display are properly maintained to reduce stock damage;
* Transfer stock between stores when needed;
* Ensure that all processes are completed thoroughly, with relevant paperwork filed in an organised way;
* Receive all deliveries and check that the stock delivered corresponds to the invoices and no stock is damaged;
* Maintain replenishment to ensure sufficient availability of products on the shop floor at all times;
* Ensure stock loss is minimised by conducting weekly rotated inventories and bi-annual stock takes. These inventories should be sent as a 'recap' on a friday to your line manager and daily to your financial coordinator;
* Resolve stock discrepancies by searching for missing products and double checking all stock internal loans (soft and hard copies) and relevant movements of stock in and out of the business;
* Responsible for pick and pack of e-commerce sales;
* Take care of returns from e-commerce sales;
* Update e-commerce sales sheets daily;
* Responsible for shipping the samples to portugal for product shoots;
* In charge of uploading samples images for e-commerce;
* Client service email.

### Profile

**KEY FOR SUCCESS**

**Experience**:

* You bring at least 2 year of professional experience in sales, within the fashion or luxury industry.

**Competencies:**

* Experience in e-commerce;
* Good team player with a passion for fashion;
* Ability to prioritise and be able to multitask;
* Ability to establish a proactive approach in tackling issues and seek to identify and implement solutions;
* A commitment to achieving and exceeding targets whilst focusing on the client's needs and experience;
* Excellent personal presentation - a celine brand ambassador;
* Understanding of retail kpis;
* A fluent level in English is essential and additional languages are an advantage.

### Additional information

**OUR COMMITMENT**

As part of our #CELINECARES approach, CELINE is committed to building an inclusive and respectful work environment where every employee can develop and thrive.

We value diversity in all its forms — origins, identities, orientations, generations, abilities and life situations — and implement concrete actions to promote inclusion. Our disability policy aims to ensure equal opportunities for all our talents, with personalized accommodations if necessary.

If you require specific assistance during the recruitment process, please do not hesitate to let us know.

At CELINE, we believe that the strength of our Maison lies in the uniqueness of our employees.

## *CELINE* MAISON

Celine is a luxury French fashion House founded in 1945 by Céline Vipiana.

